Demonstrates standard test definitions using Pest's functional syntax and Laravel's testing helpers like actingAs, get, and post.

```php
<?php

use function Pest\Laravel\{
    actingAs,
    get,
    post,
    assertDatabaseHas,
};
use App\Models\User;

test('authenticated user can access dashboard', function () {
    $user = User::factory()->create();

    actingAs($user)
        ->get('/dashboard')
        ->assertOk()
        ->assertSee('Welcome');
});

test('user registration', function () {
    post('/register', [
        'name' => 'John Doe',
        'email' => 'john@example.com',
        'password' => 'password123',
    ])
    ->assertCreated();

    assertDatabaseHas('users', [
        'email' => 'john@example.com',
    ]);
});
```

Use these imports to access common testing functions like get, post, and actingAs.

```php
use function Pest\Laravel\{
    get,
    post,
    actingAs,
    assertDatabaseHas,
};
```

In Pest Plugin Laravel v5, the `RefreshDatabase` trait is no longer automatically applied to feature tests. The stub comments it out, requiring users to explicitly uncomment the line if they need database refreshing between tests.

```php
uses(
    TestCase::class,
    // Illuminate\Foundation\Testing\RefreshDatabase::class,
)->in('Feature');
```
